{
  "_comment": [
    "The verdict's parity fixture, read by BOTH report.test.ts and",
    "backend/test_report_verdict.py. The decision lives twice -- once in",
    "report.ts for the report screen, once in backend/app/report.py for the",
    "assistant -- and an operator told GO on screen and NO-GO by the assistant",
    "has learned only not to trust either. This file is what stops that.",
    "",
    "`absent` lists keys to REMOVE from the merged summary. It exists because",
    "JavaScript's `undefined < 30` is false while Python's `None < 30` raises,",
    "so 'the field is missing' is a case in its own right and cannot be",
    "expressed by writing null: JS coerces null to 0 and would compare true.",
    "",
    "`codes`, not prose. The two copies phrase their reasons differently on",
    "purpose: the frontend interpolates numbers, the backend carries none",
    "because ai_grounding blocks any digit it did not register."
  ],
  "base": {
